So this check's expectation ("both panes whole sheet") is only true when the coupled mapping of a full sheet is also a full sheet — which happens when the two sheets have *the same* extent or when the outer is smaller than the inner... In general, "the other pane follows to its own full sheet" (documented intent in maps-3's status) is NOT what the code does. Hmm, maps-3's status said: "It ends the one gap the coupling switch left: back to the full sheet, and — when coupled — the other panes follow to their own full sheet." But the implementation follows via geographic coupling, not via reset propagation. Was that a wrong claim in the status, or was the behavior different with the old record order?

With the old pair (globe + Zürich), resetting the globe → whole globe extent → Zürich pane clamps to whole sheet → both Gesamtansicht → the check passed by accident, and the documented claim looked true. With my pair, the semantics are visible: "whole sheet" of one sheet maps to a region on the other.

