(a) geographic coupling: the other pane shows the place covered by pane 1's whole sheet — a cut-out. Keeps both panes "the same place" (consistent with the coupling promise).
(b) own full sheet: both panes show whole sheets — "reset everything" semantics. This is what the button label "Ganzes Blatt" (per pane) plus "the other panes follow to their own full sheet" claims.

The check asserts (b). The current code does (a). With the old data pair, (a) and (b) coincided.

The status file documented (b) as the intent. The check doc says "each comparison pane can go back to the whole sheet, and the link drops the cut-out". Which is better UX? Consider: with coupling on, if I reset pane 1, I probably want both sheets back to full view (a "reset the comparison" action) — especially because the button sits per pane. But under (b), the panes are no longer "the same place", which contradicts the coupling label "Ausschnitte gekoppelt". Hmm. But "Ganzes Blatt" is a per-pane action; the coupling is about pan/zoom gestures. OldMapsOnline's comparison... not sure.

